{
  "name": "Wrath of the Raging Serpent",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>While you are raging you can call down your god's fury in the form of a powerful lightning bolt when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack. The target has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 8 + your Proficiency + your STR modifier. On a failure, the creature takes 12d10 lightning damage, and half as much on a successful one. Any creature that you have Grappled has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend a use of your rage to use it again.</p>",
